The '''2026 Tour de Suisse''' was a [[road bicycle racing|road cycling]] [[cycling stage race|stage race]] that took place between 17 and 21 June in [[Switzerland]]. It was the 89th edition of the [[Tour de Suisse]] and the 25th event of the [[2026 UCI World Tour]]. It took place at the same time as the women's [[2026 Tour de Suisse Women|Tour de Suisse]], with both races using a similar route.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2026-06-17|title=Tour de Suisse Women - Peaks of Emotions|url=https://www.tourdesuisse.ch/women/|access-date=2026-06-17|website=Tour de Suisse|language=de-DE}}</ref>

The race was dominated by Slovenian rider [[Tadej Pogačar]] of {{UCI team code|UAD men|2026}}, who took the lead on stage 1 after a surprise solo attack over {{Convert|72|km|mi}}, extended his lead on the stage 4 time trial and then took further time on the mountainous final stage to confirm his overall victory. Nearly six and a half minutes behind, Ecuadorian [[Richard Carapaz]] of {{UCI team code|EFE|2026}} finished second overall, with Czech rider [[Mathias Vacek]] of {{UCI team code|LTK men|2026}} third overall, nearly seven minutes behind Pogačar.<ref>{{Cite web |date=2026-06-21 |title=Tour de Suisse 2026: Tadej Pogacar and Marlen Reusser win final stages and overall titles |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/cycling/articles/c1lye46pq96o |access-date=2026-06-22 |website=BBC Sport |language=en-GB}}</ref><ref name=":0">{{Cite web |last=Price |first=Matilda |date=2026-06-21 |title=Tour de Suisse: Tadej Pogačar powers to stage 5 win and seals commanding overall victory |url=https://www.cyclingnews.com/pro-cycling/racing/tour-de-suisse-tadej-pogacar-conquers-stage-8-to-seal-commanding-overall-victory/ |access-date=2026-06-22 |website=Cyclingnews |language=en}}</ref> 

In the other classifications, Pogačar won the points classification, Belgian rider [[Louis Vervaeke]] of {{UCI team code|SOQ|2026}} took the mountains classification, Vacek won the young rider classification and {{UCI team code|UAD men|2026|nolink=y}} won the teams classification.<ref name=":0" />

